# Socket.io Patterns

## Structure
```
sockets/
├── index.ts          # Socket.io setup
├── namespaces/       # Different namespaces (/chat, /notifications)
├── handlers/         # Event handlers per namespace
└── middlewares/      # Auth, rate limit
```

## Auth Middleware
```typescript
io.use(async (socket, next) => {
  try {
    const token = socket.handshake.auth.token;
    const user = await verifyToken(token);
    socket.data.user = user;
    next();
  } catch (err) {
    next(new Error('Unauthorized'));
  }
});
```

## Namespace Pattern
```typescript
const chatNamespace = io.of('/chat');

chatNamespace.on('connection', (socket) => {
  const user = socket.data.user;

  socket.on('message:send', async (data: SendMessageDTO) => {
    try {
      const message = await messageService.create(user.id, data);
      chatNamespace.to(data.roomId).emit('message:received', message);
    } catch (error) {
      socket.emit('error', { message: error.message });
    }
  });

  socket.on('disconnect', () => {
    // Cleanup
  });
});
```

## Event Naming
- Use `domain:action` format: `message:send`, `user:typing`, `room:joined`
- Server-to-client: `message:received`, `notification:new`
- Client-to-server: `message:send`, `room:join`

## Best Practices
- Always validate input (use same Zod schemas as REST)
- Handle disconnect/cleanup
- Use rooms for grouping (rooms, channels)
- Emit to specific users: `socket.to(socketId).emit()`
- Use rooms: `socket.join(roomId)`, `io.to(roomId).emit()`
